    "head_branch": "chore/alternating-bench",
    "head_commit_message": "chore(ci): bench alternates head and base over rounds and compares their spread\n\nOne bench run each can't tell a 5% change from the swing any change of code\nbrings: a commit against itself repeats to within 1%, but in spec 35 step 5b\ntwo commits moved phases neither touched by 5 to 20%. `bench` takes a\n`rounds` input (default 1, as before): head and base build once, then run in\nturn, head first in odd rounds and base first in even ones. The summary\nprints each phase's medians, change and ranges (bench_compare.py, tested in\ntest_bench_compare.py), marked `*` where the ranges don't overlap, then round\n1's raw output. CLAUDE.md says to use 5 rounds or more to judge a few percent.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KKUhViTbS7kfMBSZozDAco",
